The prebuilt binaries under prebuilds/ statically link the following
third-party software. The list comes from one platform's link map, the
Linux x64 musl binary's, linked exactly as shipped - every archive
member that keeps a section after --gc-sections, and the copyright lines
in its source - regenerated by native/notice-sources.sh. The other
binaries link the same OpenCV build configuration and the same addon
source; their own maps were not taken. Not linked, though OpenCV's
source tree carries them: its fonts, the MSER table, Annoy, DLPack,
FlatBuffers.

Files of OpenCV's own whose headers carry the "License Agreement for Open
Source Computer Vision Library" (3-clause BSD, below) name, besides the
holders listed under OpenCV: SpaceMIT Inc. (2025), Samson Yilma (2014),
Yechun Ruan (2021), and "Intel Corporation and others" (2009).

